## Logging Standards

### Output Modes

| Context | Format | Colours | Emojis |
|---------|--------|---------|--------|
| Console (dev) | Human-friendly | Solarized | Approved only |
| Container/CI | RFC 3339 JSON | None | ASCII text |
| File | RFC 3339 plain | None | None |

### RFC 3339 Timestamps — Always Include Timezone

```text
2025-01-20T14:30:00.123+11:00   # Local offset
2025-01-20T03:30:00.123Z        # UTC
```

### Structured Logging — Required Context

```python
logger.error(
    "Operation failed",
    user_id=user_id,           # Who
    operation="update_profile", # What
    request_id=request_id,      # Tracking
    exc_info=True               # Stack trace
)
```

### Sensitive Data Masking — ALWAYS

```python
# hyperi-pylib auto-masks:
logger.info("Connecting", password="secret123")  # → password="***MASKED***"
```

Masked patterns: passwords, API keys, bearer tokens, DB URLs, AWS keys, credit cards, JWTs, PII.

### Log Flooding Protection

| ❌ Anti-Pattern | ✅ Use Instead |
|---|---|
| `warn!`/`error!` inside per-message loops | Sampled logging (1/1000) + metrics counter |
| Logging sustained state every check | State-transition logging (log change only) |
| Retry loop logging per attempt | Log first failure + recovery only |
| `debug!` formatting large structs unconditionally | Level guard: `if enabled!(DEBUG) { debug!(...) }` |
| `info!` in per-request handlers | `debug!` for request-level; metrics for visibility |

