## Git Standards

### Default Branch: `main` (never `master`)

### Branch Flow

```
feature-branch → merge → main → PR → release
```

**NEVER:** checkout `release`, commit directly to `release`, push to `release` without PR, force-push `release`.

### Branch Naming

```text
<type>/<issue-ref>/<short-description>   # feat/AI-123/add-cursor-support
<type>/<short-description>                # fix/memory-leak
```

Types: feat, fix, docs, test, chore, ci, cleanup, data, debt, design, infra, meta, ops, perf, refactor, review, sec, spike, ui, hotfix

### Commit Types (Conventional Commits)

**Trigger version bumps:**

| Type | Use | Bump |
|------|-----|------|
| `feat:` | New user-facing feature (**RARELY** — AI exaggerates importance) | MINOR |
| `fix:` | Bug fix, improvement, cleanup (**DEFAULT** — use most of the time) | PATCH |
| `perf:` | Performance optimisation | PATCH |
| `refactor:` | Code restructure (no functional change) | PATCH |
| `hotfix:` | Critical production fix | PATCH |
| `sec:` | Security fix | PATCH |

**No version bump:**

| Type | Use |
|------|-----|
| `docs:` | Documentation |
| `test:` | Test coverage |
| `chore:` | Dependencies, config |
| `ci:` | CI/CD workflows |
| `infra:` | Infrastructure |
| `ops:` | Operational maintenance |
| `cleanup:` | Remove deprecated code |
| `debt:` | Technical debt |
| `spike:` | Research/PoC |

**`BREAKING CHANGE:` in footer → MAJOR bump. NEVER write automatically — always ask user.**

### Commit Message Rules

- 50 chars max subject, lowercase after type, no period, imperative mood
- Body: explain WHY not WHAT, wrap at 72 chars
- `Fixes #123`, `Refs #456` in footer
- No emojis in commits. EVER.

### AI Commit Guidance

- ALWAYS show proposed message and request approval (mature projects)
- ALWAYS use human-like, concise messages. One line preferred, 3 max.
- ALWAYS err conservative on type (if you think `feat:`, it's probably `fix:`)
- ALWAYS `git pull --rebase` before push (semantic-release creates version commits)
- ALWAYS seek approval before ANY push — show commit list + projected version bump

