## Design Principles (Summary)

| Principle | Key Rule |
|-----------|----------|
| **SRP** | Each class/function has ONE reason to change |
| **OCP** | Open for extension, closed for modification — extend via composition/inheritance |
| **LSP** | Subtypes must be substitutable for base types — don't break contracts |
| **ISP** | Split fat interfaces into small, focused ones |
| **DIP** | Depend on abstractions, not concrete implementations |
| **DRY** | Extract after 3+ duplicates (Rule of Three). Wrong abstraction > duplication. |
| **KISS** | Simple > clever. `config = load_config("config.yaml")` not factory-of-factory |
| **YAGNI** | Only build what's needed NOW. Don't build plugin systems for one plugin. |

