## PKI & Cryptography

### Security Profiles

| Profile | TLS Cert | SSH | Use For |
|---------|----------|-----|---------|
| **prod** (corporate default) | ECDSA P-384 | Ed25519 | Production, customer-facing |
| devtest | ECDSA P-256 | Ed25519 | Local dev, staging |
| highsec | P-384 → ML-DSA (CNSA 2.0) | Ed25519 + ML-KEM | Federal/defence contracts |

### Non-Negotiable

- TLS 1.2 minimum, TLS 1.3 preferred
- No SHA-1, MD5, DES, 3DES, RC4, CBC mode
- Private keys never in git (`.gitignore`: `*.key`, `*.pem`, `*.p12`)
- File permissions: 600 for private keys, 700 for `.ssh`

```bash
# SSH key (all profiles)
ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -C "user@hyperi.io"

# TLS cert (prod)
openssl ecparam -genkey -name secp384r1 -out server.key
openssl req -x509 -new -key server.key -out server.crt -days 365 -sha384 \
    -subj "/CN=app.example.com/O=HyperI/C=AU"
```

